it's been declared an environmental  emergency crude oil washing ashore after  a devastating spill along the peruvian  coast near lima  the tsunami caused by the volcanic  eruption near tonga on january 15th  apparently ruptured an underwater  pipeline as a spanish reptile oil tanker  was unloading crude at a refinery  causing the disaster  an investigation is underway  authorities say the challenge to contain  and clean the estimated 6000 barrels  dumped may be impossible to accomplish  but teams of volunteers at the cavero  beach near the main spill area are doing  their best  a few kilometers away at the bay of  ancon another team is recovering only 20  barrels of the spill per day  it's really not much just a grain of  sand the attention on the cleanup  campaign should be more aggressive  concerned university students have  teamed up to save some species  for now we are cleaning and seeing what  we can do with these crabs because we  are not going to be so heartless and  leave them there  environmental authorities say the damage  now extends 3 000 square kilometers  affecting ancon bay's rich biodiversity  from the fisherman's protected islands  to the coastline fauna  we're about four kilometers off the  coast of the bay of ancon and here the  water is completely under a blanket of  oil the ocean current is helping to  spread it even further making it more  difficult to clean  [Music]  to contain its advance environmental  authorities have cordoned off a small  bay area fisherman avelino ramirez says  more than 800 families who need it for  their living now have nothing to sell  everything has stopped unknown as going  out to sea because we know that the fish  is unusable and will be contaminated  it's surprising that repsol has not had  a contingency plan  on thursday president pedro castillo  declared the environmental emergency  describing the oil spill as the most  worrying ecological disaster in recent  times some are blaming repsol but the  company says it had no warning of the  tsunami and is not responsible  while judicial authorities opened an  investigation experts say reversing the  damage is impossible especially with so  much to be done and with so few  volunteers at work on the ground  mariana sanchez
 

